agm: 1.0
package: backend.tasks
version: 0.1.0
title: Backend Engineering Tasks

node backend.ticket.migrate_to_uuid_pks
type: ticket
summary: migrate all public-facing entity endpoints to use UUID primary keys instead of sequential integers
title: Migrate to UUID Primary Keys in Public API
description: Replace sequential integer IDs in public API responses with UUID surrogate keys.
priority: high
stability: high
detail:
  Sequential integer IDs in public API responses expose row counts and enable
  enumeration attacks. This ticket covers the migration of the four primary
  domain entities: User, Invoice, Order, and PaymentMethod.

  Migration plan:
    1. Add uuid column to each table, default gen_random_uuid()
    2. Backfill existing rows
    3. Update API serializers to emit uuid instead of id
    4. Dual-emit both fields for one release cycle
    5. Deprecate integer id field
    6. Remove integer id from API response after deprecation window

notes:
  The internal integer ID remains as the physical primary key for join performance.
  Only the external representation changes.
